-- Forte_Cooldown/Core/Engine.lua
-- Class-agnostic cooldown engine. Reads ForteXorcist.Data.<Class> (generated by
-- tools/gen_spell_data.py) and tracks the player's own cooldowns.
--
-- Why it is built this way (see docs/engine-notes.md for sources):
--  * On WoW Forever a cooldown read in combat can come back as a "secret"
--    value. Comparing or doing arithmetic on one throws. So every live read
--    goes through Compat.PlainOrNil, and a nil (secret) read never overwrites
--    what we already know.
--  * Your own UNIT_SPELLCAST_SUCCEEDED stays readable in combat. A successful
--    cast of a tracked spell starts a *predicted* entry at GetTime() with the
--    best known duration -- learned from a real out-of-combat read when we
--    have one, else the generated data's base cooldown.
--  * Whenever a read *is* plain (always out of combat, sometimes in combat),
--    it wins: the entry is re-anchored to the real start/duration and that
--    duration is learned (persisted) for the next prediction.
--  * Tracking is keyed by spell NAME, not ID: the generated data stores the
--    highest-rank ID, but a lower-level character knows a lower rank with a
--    different ID. C_Spell resolves a name to whatever rank the player knows.
--
-- Entry provenance (`entry.source`):
--  * "cast"  started by OnCast from our own (plain) UNIT_SPELLCAST_SUCCEEDED.
--  * "read"  anchored/confirmed by a plain cooldown read (OnRead) -- an
--            anchoring read also *certifies* an entry created by "edge".
--  * "edge"  started by OnActiveEdge from the NeverSecret isActive/isOnGCD
--            booleans when the cast event's spellID arrived secret (PLAN §8
--            mitigation 2). Same predicted BestDuration window as "cast",
--            but an "edge" entry that no plain read ever anchored never
--            pops ready (inferred-entries rule, PLAN §3.2); it is swept in
--            silence when its window lapses.
--  * "duration"
--            anchored by OnReadDuration from a plain LuaDurationObject of
--            C_Spell.GetSpellCooldownDuration -- the one cooldown-timing
--            read with NO output-restriction annotation
--            (docs/research/secrets-unknowns.md §2). Always `anchored`.
--
-- The read ladder (docs/research/secrets-unknowns.md §2 + §5, PLAN §8
-- mitigations; the launch-day evidence is Engine counts in FX.db.diag
-- .readTiers, printed by `/fx status`):
--  1. NUMERIC  OnRead / OnReadCharges -- the full truth, may be secret.
--  2. BOOLEAN  OnReadActive -- the NeverSecret isActive/isOnGCD pair: detects
--              an EARLY end (a reset/proc: a predicted entry the engine says
--              is no longer running) and a cooldown START no event named.
--              Booleans carry no numbers, so they never teach a duration;
--              the numbers of a spell they cleared stay predicted.
--  3. DURATION OnReadDuration -- the unannotated duration object: an exact
--              endTime (+ a learnable total) even when tier 1 is secret.
-- Tiers 2/3 are opportunistic: each does its one thing on a plain signal and
-- leaves everything else to tier 1. `FX.SecretState` only says when tier 1 is
-- not worth asking at all (skip work), never what is true.
--
-- Multi-charge model (owner ruling 2026-11-01: multi-charge is MISSING in
-- the original -- built new; the DISPLAY draws charge counts later, this
-- layer only exposes the data):
--  * `tracked[name].maxCharges` is set at RUNTIME by Engine:DetectCharges
--    from the NeverSecret SpellChargeInfo.maxCharges -- no spell data.
--  * A charge spell's entry carries `charges = { max, current, nextAt }`:
--    `current` charges are castable right now, `nextAt` is when the NEXT
--    charge lands (nil = bar full). `entry.rechargeEnd` mirrors `nextAt`
--    for the display; a charge entry's start/duration/endTime describe the
--    LAST cast's window, and the sweep reuses `duration` as the per-charge
--    recharge length (anchored reads set it from the real charge-cooldown
--    pair, predictions from BestDuration).
--  * A cast consumes one charge: current = max(current - 1, 0); the first
--    cast of a draining bar arms the recharge clock at now + BestDuration.
--  * Sweep advances the clock: while nextAt <= now, current is incremented
--    and nextAt += duration (nextAt = nil once current == max). The entry
--    expires -- and, like any "edge" entry, pops ONLY once the FULL bar is
--    back (current >= max). While current > 0 the spell is castable: the
--    entry is NOT "on cooldown" -- the display must keep such rows off the
--    cooling/splash treatment and use `charges`/`maxCharges`/`rechargeEnd`
--    for the count, and the "ready" pop belongs to the full-bar moment.
--  * Sorted() rows expose `charges` (the CURRENT count, nil = not a charge
--    spell) and `maxCharges` alongside them.
--  * OnReadCharges (from C_Spell.GetSpellCharges) re-anchors: `current` from
--    the plain currentCharges, `nextAt` from the plain
--    cooldownStartTime + cooldownDuration; any secret component leaves the
--    clock model untouched. A plain full-bar read CLEARS the entry. A
--    drained bar the read catches with NO clock at all (secret pair, no
--    previous charges model) arms one at `now + BestDuration` -- OnCast's
--    arming rule -- because a clockless charge entry can never satisfy the
--    Sweep and would ride `entries` forever (m3, review 2026-11-01). For a
--    charge spell the plain GetSpellCooldown "ready" read never clears
--    (its last-cast window lapses mid-bar): the charge read owns the
--    lifecycle, and OnRead only ever ANCHORS.
--
-- Everything here is plain Lua state + functions so it can be unit-tested
-- under wow-ui-sim without driving real combat (see tests/).

ForteXorcist = ForteXorcist or {}
local FX = ForteXorcist

FX.Cooldown = FX.Cooldown or {}
local Engine = {}
FX.Cooldown.Engine = Engine

-- Below this many seconds a "cooldown" is just the global cooldown; never track it.
-- 2.99 (not 2.5) matches the original ForteXorcist `FW.Default.IgnoreCooldown`:
-- anything under a 3 s GCD band is noise, not a tracked cooldown.
Engine.MIN_COOLDOWN = 2.99

-- Fresh-prediction read-lag grace (seconds). The law of every read tier: a
-- read taken right after our own cast event can still report the PRE-cast
-- state, so a "ready" signal inside this window proves nothing. Core/Items.lua
-- carries the same 1.6 as its file-local `PREDICTION_GRACE` for the item side
-- (owner law, single value; kept local there so that file stays self-contained).
Engine.PREDICTION_GRACE = 1.6

Engine.tracked = {}   -- [name] = { name, dataId, baseDuration, maxCharges? (runtime, DetectCharges) }
-- [name] = { name, start, duration, endTime, predicted, source =
--            "cast"|"read"|"edge", anchored?, charges? = {max, current,
--            nextAt}, rechargeEnd? = nextAt, category? ("Item"/"Potion" --
--            set only by Core/Items.lua entries; rows default "Spell"),
--            icon? (item texture; nil = Timeline resolves the spell icon) }
--            -- see file header
Engine.entries = {}
-- Four feeds write this table, in three key shapes: the data NAME (a spell,
-- from the tracked set, and a tracked item), `<name>#<buffId>` (a proc ICD
-- window, Core/Procs.lua) and `<name>#<slot>` (a weapon-enchant window,
-- Core/Enchants.lua). `Engine:Build` empties it -- it is the Build's own
-- contract -- and the caller decides what rides the wipe: a same-class
-- rebuild carries back every window whose key the fresh state still tracks
-- (Forte_Cooldown/Module.lua's rebuild carry, FX7a), a class change starts it
-- clean. The rows below are the entry shape (file header).
Engine.learned = {}   -- [name] = seconds, persisted via Engine:AttachStorage

--- Point learned durations at a SavedVariables-backed table so they survive reloads.
function Engine:AttachStorage(tbl)
    self.learned = tbl
end

local function TitleCase(classFile)
    if not classFile then return nil end
    return classFile:sub(1, 1):upper() .. classFile:sub(2):lower()
end

--- Build the tracked set from the generated data for `classFile` ("HUNTER", ...).
--- `isKnown(name)` decides whether the player has the spell; injectable for tests.
--- Returns the number of spells tracked, or nil + reason if there is no data.
--- The third result is the CLASS CHANGE: `classFile` differs from the class
--- this Engine last built. `entries` is wiped either way -- the tracked set is
--- the fresh build's own -- and the caller decides what rides the wipe (the
--- rebuild carry, Forte_Cooldown/Module.lua): a same-class rebuild is a re-read
--- of the known set, so its running windows are the same question they were,
--- while a class change is a fresh question with nothing to carry across.
function Engine:Build(classFile, isKnown)
    local classChanged = self.builtClass ~= classFile
    self.builtClass = classFile
    wipe(self.tracked)
    wipe(self.entries)
    local key = TitleCase(classFile)
    local data = key and FX.Data and FX.Data[key]
    if not data then
        return nil, "no generated data for class " .. tostring(classFile),
            classChanged
    end
    local n = 0
    for id, spell in pairs(data) do
        local cd = spell.cooldownMs and spell.cooldownMs / 1000
        if cd and cd >= self.MIN_COOLDOWN and spell.name
            and not spell.racial and isKnown(spell.name) then
            -- `racial = true` rows are the racials group (spell lists, wave
            -- M3a): the SAME generated data, but tracked by AddExtras after
            -- Build (the known-gate there is id-aware, `IsPlayerSpell(id)`,
            -- because a racial is known by race, not by class spells).
            -- Build's count stays the class-kit count its tests pin.
            self.tracked[spell.name] = { name = spell.name, dataId = id, baseDuration = cd }
            n = n + 1
        end
    end
    return n, nil, classChanged
end

--- The racials (the generated `racial = true` rows of the class data —
--- Berserking 20554, Rapid Regeneration 1260270, the Hunter's Summon Hawk
--- 1293527, wave M3a), added AFTER Build by the Module's Rebuild so Build's
--- contract (class kit only) and its count tests stay exactly as they were.
--- Review-10 M2/m4 retired the hand-kept, ID-keyed `Engine.RACIALS` table
--- this replaces: its English `name` keys broke the locale law (names
--- entering this Engine ride `Locale.CanonicalName` and the generated data
--- is the alias source — a hand-keyed English name on a deDE client was
--- compared against a canonicalized client name and never matched, so the
--- racial was never tracked); its hand-typed ids (20554/1260270/1293241)
--- bypassed tools/gen_spell_data.py and every data refresh. The rows now
--- ride the generated data (measured 180 s cooldowns cited in
--- tools/overrides_devnotes_2026-11-03.json; the Summon Hawk id rides the
--- `_pins` law at the store's captured Rank 4, NOT the 70425-era 1293241
--- id-slot the hand table froze), the NAME key is the data's, and `shares`
--- ("Summon Hawk" -> "Arcane Shot", the store's shared category 1173) is
--- the data's. Tracked only when the player knows the spell; returns how
--- many were added.
function Engine:AddExtras(isKnown)
    local key = TitleCase(self.builtClass)
    local data = key and FX.Data and FX.Data[key]
    if not data then return 0 end
    local n = 0
    for id, spell in pairs(data) do
        local cd = spell.racial and spell.cooldownMs and spell.cooldownMs / 1000
        local known = cd and cd >= self.MIN_COOLDOWN and spell.name
            and (isKnown(spell.name)
                or (FX.Compat.IsPlayerSpell and FX.Compat.IsPlayerSpell(id)))
        if known then
            self.tracked[spell.name] = { name = spell.name, dataId = id,
                baseDuration = cd, shares = spell.shares }
            n = n + 1
        end
    end
    return n
end

--- Runtime multi-charge detection (owner ruling 2026-11-01: multi-charge is
--- MISSING in the original -- nothing in the generated data says which
--- spells have charges, so the flag is measured live, never declared).
--- Reads the NeverSecret SpellChargeInfo.maxCharges for every tracked name;
--- >1 marks `tracked[name].maxCharges`. `readCharges(spellName)` is
--- injectable for tests and defaults to the live C_Spell read.
function Engine:DetectCharges(readCharges)
    readCharges = readCharges or FX.Compat.GetSpellCharges
    if not readCharges then return end
    for name, t in pairs(self.tracked) do
        -- pcall: a live charges read can throw (secret values propagate as
        -- a raise). The flag is best-effort; one spell blowing up is not.
        local ok, info = pcall(readCharges, name)
        local max = ok and info and FX.Compat.PlainOrNil(info.maxCharges)
        if type(max) == "number" and max > 1 then
            t.maxCharges = max
        end
    end
end

--- Best duration we have for a tracked spell: learned beats generated base.
function Engine:BestDuration(name)
    local learned = self.learned[name]
    if learned and learned >= self.MIN_COOLDOWN then return learned end
    local t = self.tracked[name]
    return t and t.baseDuration
end

--- A successful cast of `name` at `now`. Starts (or restarts) a predicted
--- entry. For a charge spell the cast consumes one charge: current =
--- max(current - 1, 0), and the first cast of a draining bar arms the
--- recharge clock at now + BestDuration (file header). A fresh cast clears
--- any prior read-certification (`anchored`). Returns the entry, or nil if
--- `name` isn't tracked.
function Engine:OnCast(name, now, _partner)
    local t = self.tracked[name]
    if not t then return nil end
    local duration = self:BestDuration(name)
    if not duration then return nil end
    local e = self.entries[name] or { name = name }
    e.start, e.duration, e.endTime, e.predicted = now, duration, now + duration, true
    e.source, e.anchored = "cast", nil
    if t.maxCharges then
        local c = e.charges
        if not c then
            c = { max = t.maxCharges, current = t.maxCharges }
            e.charges = c
        end
        c.current = math.max(c.current - 1, 0)
        if c.nextAt == nil then c.nextAt = now + duration end
    end
    self.entries[name] = e
    -- Shared cooldown: the partner spell goes on cooldown with this one.
    if not _partner then
        for pname, pt in pairs(self.tracked) do
            if pname ~= name and (t.shares == pname or pt.shares == name) then
                self:OnCast(pname, now, true)
            end
        end
    end
    return e
end

--- A live cooldown read for `name`. `start`/`duration` may be secret (pass raw;
--- this guards them). A plain, real cooldown re-anchors the entry and is learned;
--- a plain "not on cooldown" read clears it; a secret read changes nothing.
--- Returns "anchored", "cleared", "secret" or "ignored".
function Engine:OnRead(name, start, duration, now)
    local t = self.tracked[name]
    if not t then return "ignored" end
    start = FX.Compat.PlainOrNil(start)
    duration = FX.Compat.PlainOrNil(duration)
    -- A number is what this tier needs. The nil-only check used to live here
    -- let a NON-number through into the `start > 0` compare below, and the
    -- compare on a string raises (measured in wow-ui-sim 2026-11-02: on a
    -- name-keyed read whose table path raised, the legacy multi-return
    -- `GetSpellCooldown` hands strings -- "attempt to compare number with
    -- string" out of Engine.lua, i.e. out of the whole 1 Hz pass). A read we
    -- cannot do arithmetic on is exactly what "secret" means here.
    if type(start) ~= "number" or type(duration) ~= "number" then return "secret" end

    if start > 0 and duration >= self.MIN_COOLDOWN then
        local e = self.entries[name] or { name = name }
        e.start, e.duration, e.endTime, e.predicted = start, duration, start + duration, false
        -- A plain read is the certification: it re-anchors the window and
        -- vouches for an "edge" entry, unlocking its ready pop (header).
        -- Charges are left to OnReadCharges -- the charge read owns the bar.
        e.source, e.anchored = "read", true
        self.entries[name] = e
        -- Learn only from a full-length read: a read whose start we did not see
        -- still carries the full duration, so this is safe either way.
        self.learned[name] = duration
        return "anchored"
    end

    -- Plain read says "ready" (or GCD only). Trust it only if our own entry
    -- isn't a fresh prediction still inside its window -- the GCD can mask
    -- a just-started cooldown for a moment after the cast.
    local e = self.entries[name]
    if t.maxCharges then
        -- A charge spell whose plain GetSpellCooldown window lapsed is NOT
        -- ready: it is mid-bar. The charges read (OnReadCharges) owns the
        -- lifecycle of a charge entry -- this read only ever anchors.
        return "ignored"
    end
    if e and e.predicted and now < e.endTime
        and (now - e.start) < self.PREDICTION_GRACE then
        return "ignored"
    end
    self.entries[name] = nil
    return "cleared"
end

--- A live charges read for `name` (raw fields of C_Spell.GetSpellCharges;
--- guard them here). Plain `currentCharges` re-anchors the bar's `current`;
--- a plain `cooldownStartTime`/`cooldownDuration` pair re-anchors `nextAt`
--- (when the next charge lands) and the entry window -- for a charge entry
--- `duration` is the per-charge recharge the sweep steps by. A plain
--- full-bar read means the spell is READY: the entry is cleared. A secret
--- `currentCharges` leaves the clock model untouched (secret pairs keep the
--- existing nextAt). Returns "anchored", "cleared", "secret" or "ignored".
function Engine:OnReadCharges(name, currentCharges, cooldownStartTime, cooldownDuration, now)
    local t = self.tracked[name]
    if not t or not t.maxCharges then return "ignored" end
    currentCharges = FX.Compat.PlainOrNil(currentCharges)
    if currentCharges == nil then return "secret" end
    if currentCharges >= t.maxCharges then
        -- Full bar plain-visible: nothing on cooldown, nothing to model.
        self.entries[name] = nil
        return "cleared"
    end
    local e = self.entries[name]
    if not e then
        local bd = self:BestDuration(name)
        if not bd then return "ignored" end
        e = { name = name, start = now, duration = bd, endTime = now + bd }
        self.entries[name] = e
    end
    local start = FX.Compat.PlainOrNil(cooldownStartTime)
    local duration = FX.Compat.PlainOrNil(cooldownDuration)
    local prev = e.charges
    local c = { max = t.maxCharges, current = math.max(currentCharges, 0) }
    e.charges = c
    -- No MIN_COOLDOWN floor on the pair: a per-charge recharge shorter than
    -- a GCD band is a real charge bar, not GCD noise (the floor governs
    -- which SPELLS we track, not how a tracked bar recharges).
    if start ~= nil and duration ~= nil and start > 0 and duration > 0 then
        -- The Blizzard charge pair is fact: window and clock ride it.
        c.nextAt = start + duration
        e.start, e.duration, e.endTime = start, duration, start + duration
        e.predicted, e.source, e.anchored = false, "read", true
    elseif prev then
        -- Secret pair: keep the clock model; the charges read still
        -- certifies the bar's count.
        c.nextAt = prev.nextAt
    end
    if c.nextAt == nil and c.current < c.max then
        -- m3: a drained bar with no clock to inherit -- the pair was secret
        -- AND there was no previous charges model (the entry is fresh from
        -- this read). The charge Sweep advances only via `nextAt` and pops
        -- only at the full bar, so a clockless drained bar can never be
        -- `done`: the entry would ride in `entries` for the rest of the
        -- session. Arm the recharge clock exactly like OnCast arms it --
        -- the best known duration from `now` -- so the bar always finishes.
        local bd = self:BestDuration(name)
        if bd then
            c.nextAt = now + bd
            if not e.duration then e.duration = bd end
        end
    end
    return "anchored"
end

--- The active-edge fallback (PLAN §8 mitigation 2): when a cast's spellID
--- arrives secret, in-combat prediction has no event to ride on -- but
--- SpellCooldownInfo.isActive / .isOnGCD are NeverSecret, so Module's read
--- pass can see a tracked spell's cooldown RUNNING (not the GCD) and call
--- this. It creates the same predicted BestDuration window OnCast makes,
--- tagged source = "edge": a never-anchored "edge" entry never pops ready
--- (inferred-entries rule, PLAN §3.2); it is swept in silence when its
--- window lapses. Returns the entry, or nil if `name` is untracked, has a
--- live entry, or no duration is known.
function Engine:OnActiveEdge(name, now)
    if not self.tracked[name] then return nil end
    if self.entries[name] then return nil end
    local duration = self:BestDuration(name)
    if not duration then return nil end
    local e = { name = name, start = now, duration = duration,
                endTime = now + duration, predicted = true, source = "edge" }
    self.entries[name] = e
    return e
end

--- TIER 2 -- the boolean ready tier. `isActive` / `isOnGCD` are the raw
--- SpellCooldownInfo booleans: DOCS `NeverSecret`
--- (`SpellCooldownInfo @SpellSharedDocumentation.lua:18`, cited
--- docs/research/secrets-unknowns.md §2), so they answer in a combat
--- lockdown of the numbers this file's numeric tier goes blind on. They are
--- still routed through PlainOrNil: a claim about an *output annotation* is
--- not a claim about a runtime value, and `x == true` on a secret raises.
--- `now` is a plain GetTime() frame time, never a read.
---
--- What the two bits can prove, and nothing else:
---  * `isActive == false` with `isOnGCD ~= true` on OUR OWN PREDICTION that
---    is older than `PREDICTION_GRACE` -- the read-lag law of `OnRead`: a
---    read right after a cast can still report the pre-cast window, so the
---    bit only speaks once the cast has had time to land. Then the real
---    cooldown ended EARLY (a reset, a proc, a clear) and the prediction is
---    the only thing keeping the icon on the bar. The window is landed right
---    here (`endTime = now`, `duration` kept consistent with `start`), so the
---    next `Sweep` retires the entry with the NORMAL ready pop -- the
---    inferred-entries law stays in the Sweep: a never-anchored "edge" entry
---    still dies in silence.
---  * `isActive == true` with no live entry -- a cooldown is running that no
---    cast event named (the secret-spellID case): the existing
---    `OnActiveEdge` fallback, tagged source = "edge".
--- Anything else -- a "read"/"duration" window the numbers own, a charge bar
--- the charges read owns (file header), a plain-true with a live entry, a
--- GCD-only active, a secret/absent bit -- leaves the state alone. Booleans
--- carry NO numbers: this tier never learns a duration.
--- Returns "cleared" | "edge" | "kept" | "ignored".
function Engine:OnReadActive(name, isActive, isOnGCD, now)
    if not self.tracked[name] then return "ignored" end
    isActive = FX.Compat.PlainOrNil(isActive)
    isOnGCD = FX.Compat.PlainOrNil(isOnGCD)
    local e = self.entries[name]
    if isActive == false then
        if not e then return "ignored" end
        -- The GCD's own activity is not a statement about this spell.
        if isOnGCD == true then return "kept" end
        -- A charge bar is the charges read's lifecycle (file header); the
        -- GetSpellCooldown booleans say nothing trustworthy mid-bar.
        if e.charges then return "kept" end
        -- Only a *predicted* window: a plain read's entry is the numbers'
        -- own business (its next plain read, or the Sweep, retires it).
        if not e.predicted then return "kept" end
        if (now - e.start) < self.PREDICTION_GRACE then return "kept" end
        e.endTime, e.duration = now, now - e.start
        return "cleared"
    end
    if isActive == true then
        if e then return "kept" end
        if isOnGCD == true then return "ignored" end
        local created = self:OnActiveEdge(name, now)
        return created and "edge" or "ignored"
    end
    return "kept"
end

--- TIER 3 -- the opportunistic exact anchor. `remaining` / `total` are the
--- raw `GetRemainingDuration()` / `GetTotalDuration()` of the
--- LuaDurationObject of `C_Spell.GetSpellCooldownDuration` (the caller
--- probed `HasSecretValues()` and passed only a plain object's numbers; the
--- values are guarded HERE too, so no caller can forget). Both are
--- documented **Seconds** (`LuaDurationObjectAPIDocumentation.lua:270` /
--- `:318`, cited at the Compat seam) -- the scale the entry model already
--- lives on, so no conversion happens anywhere.
---
--- A plain object is engine-sourced timing, which is what `OnRead`'s
--- "anchored" branch has always certified, so the entry is re-anchored
--- exactly like that: `endTime = now + remaining`, `start = endTime -
--- total`, `duration = total`, `source = "duration"`, `anchored = true`,
--- `predicted = false`. With no readable total only the END is fact: `start`
--- is kept and the window's own length absorbs the difference
--- (`duration = endTime - start`), which keeps the
--- `start + duration == endTime` invariant the Timeline draws on. A full
--- total is learned exactly under `OnRead`'s law (a real length, never a
--- GCD-band value). A drained charge bar's clock follows the real end (`+
--- rechargeEnd`, the file header's mirror). With no entry at all an anchor
--- needs the total to have a start -- without it, nothing.
--- Returns "anchored" | "ignored".
function Engine:OnReadDuration(name, remaining, total, now)
    if not self.tracked[name] then return "ignored" end
    remaining = FX.Compat.PlainOrNil(remaining)
    total = FX.Compat.PlainOrNil(total)
    if type(remaining) ~= "number" or remaining <= 0 then return "ignored" end
    local endTime = now + remaining
    -- A total only counts as a length when it is a real cooldown length
    -- (the OnRead >= MIN_COOLDOWN law); a GCD-band total is the GCD's, not
    -- this spell's, so it must not be learned nor written into the window.
    local full = (type(total) == "number" and total >= self.MIN_COOLDOWN)
        and total or nil
    local e = self.entries[name]
    if not e then
        if not full then return "ignored" end
        e = { name = name }
        self.entries[name] = e
    end
    local duration = full or (endTime - (e.start or now))
    if duration <= 0 then duration = remaining end
    e.start, e.duration, e.endTime = endTime - duration, duration, endTime
    e.predicted, e.source, e.anchored = false, "duration", true
    if e.charges and e.charges.nextAt ~= nil then
        e.charges.nextAt = endTime
        e.rechargeEnd = endTime
    end
    if full then self.learned[name] = full end
    return "anchored"
end

--- Remove entries whose time ran out. Returns an array of names that just
--- became ready (file header): a plain window pops at its endTime; a charge
--- entry pops only once the FULL bar is back; a never-anchored "edge" entry
--- is removed in silence -- an inferred entry never claims the ready moment
--- (PLAN §3.2).
--- `popInfo` (m3, CodeReview4) is the caller's OPTIONAL scratch map: when
--- given, the popping entry's `{ duration, icon, category }` snapshot is
--- written to `popInfo[<popped name>]` right here, in the one place that
--- already touches the entry before deleting it. The pop consumers need
--- the facts of the window that just ended and the entry is gone after
--- this loop; capturing at the pop site is why Module:ProcessReadyPops no
--- longer pre-snapshots every live entry on every 10 Hz tick.
function Engine:Sweep(now, out, popInfo)
    out = out or {}
    for name, e in pairs(self.entries) do
        local c, done = e.charges, nil
        if c then
            -- Charge clock (header): one charge lands per recharge window.
            while c.nextAt ~= nil and c.nextAt <= now do
                c.current = c.current + 1
                c.nextAt = (c.current < c.max) and (c.nextAt + e.duration) or nil
            end
            done = c.current >= c.max
        else
            done = now >= e.endTime
        end
        if done then
            self.entries[name] = nil
            if not (e.source == "edge" and not e.anchored) then
                -- The pop names the entry for the Display's `_ready` queue
                -- and the event, and both speak the DISPLAY name. Spell/
                -- item entries key by that name already; the weapon-
                -- enchant entries key `<name>#<slot>` (Core/Enchants.lua,
                -- CodeReview2 n3), so the key is not necessarily the name.
                local popName = e.name or name
                out[#out + 1] = popName
                if popInfo then
                    local info = popInfo[popName]
                    if not info then
                        info = {}
                        popInfo[popName] = info
                    end
                    info.duration, info.icon, info.category =
                        e.duration, e.icon, e.category
                    -- TEST MODE (`/fx` Core/TestMode.lua): the pop consumer
                    -- needs to know a popping entry is a synthetic one, and
                    -- this is the last site where the entry itself is in hand
                    -- (the loop below deletes it). A tag of OUR entry table,
                    -- never a client read.
                    info._source = e._source
                end
            end
        end
    end
    return out
end

--- Build/reuse the display ROW view of an entry: the entry's own fields
--- plus the charge trio flattened -- `charges` = the CURRENT castable
--- count (nil = not a charge spell), `maxCharges`, `rechargeEnd` = when the
--- next charge lands. Rows are cached on the entry so the 10 Hz pass
--- allocates nothing (the row outlives its entry by design: both die on the
--- next Build). Rows, not live entries, travel to the Display so its reads
--- cannot mutate the bar state.
--- Display tags (cross-worker contract 2026-11-01): `category` is the
--- row's EFFECTIVE category -- item entries carry "Item"/"Potion" (set by
--- Core/Items.lua), a spell's tracked row may carry a per-spell `fxClass`
--- override (the Timeline's documented classification knob), the rest
--- default "Spell". `icon` is nil for spells (the Timeline's own spell-icon
--- resolution then applies), a texture for items.
local function rowFor(e)
    local r = e.row
    if not r then
        r = {}
        e.row = r
    end
    r.name, r.start, r.duration, r.endTime = e.name, e.start, e.duration, e.endTime
    r.predicted, r.source = e.predicted, e.source
    local c = e.charges
    r.charges, r.maxCharges, r.rechargeEnd = c and c.current, c and c.max, c and c.nextAt
    local t = Engine.tracked[e.name]
    r.category = e.category or (t and t.fxClass) or "Spell"
    r.icon = e.icon
    return r
end

--- Entries sorted by soonest-ready first. Reuses `out` to avoid per-tick
--- garbage. An entry whose charge bar has current > 0 is NOT on cooldown
--- (castable; header) and stays out of this cooling list -- the display
--- reads the charge count off a charge entry only while the bar is drained
--- (`charges` = 0, `rechargeEnd` = the next charge landing).
function Engine:Sorted(out)
    out = out or {}
    wipe(out)
    for _, e in pairs(self.entries) do
        if not (e.charges and e.charges.current > 0) then
            out[#out + 1] = rowFor(e)
        end
    end
    table.sort(out, function(a, b)
        if a.endTime ~= b.endTime then return a.endTime < b.endTime end
        return a.name < b.name
    end)
    return out
end
